# NOTE: since the operator console exists, this file is OPTIONAL. Everything below
# except STORAGE_DIR / SIGNFLOW_SECRET / PORT can be set in the browser under Admin,
# and values set there override these. Keep env vars for container deployments.

# Copy this file to .env and fill it in to enable email sending.
# Without it, the app still works — signing links are shown in the UI to copy.

# --- Option A: Microsoft 365 / Outlook work email ---
# Uses your existing work email to send the signing links.
# If emails fail to send, your Microsoft admin needs to switch on
# "Authenticated SMTP" for your mailbox (Microsoft 365 admin center →
# Users → your user → Mail → Manage email apps → tick Authenticated SMTP).
# SMTP_HOST=smtp.office365.com
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_USER=yourname@softshala.com
# SMTP_PASS=your-email-password
# FROM_EMAIL="SignFlow <yourname@softshala.com>"

# --- Option B: Gmail (free, up to ~500 emails/day) ---
# 1. Turn on 2-Step Verification on your Google account
# 2. Go to https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords and create an App Password
SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
SMTP_PORT=465
SMTP_USER=yourname@gmail.com
SMTP_PASS=your-16-char-app-password
FROM_EMAIL="SignFlow <yourname@gmail.com>"

# --- Option C: Brevo (free 300 emails/day, no Gmail account needed) ---
# Sign up at brevo.com → SMTP & API → SMTP keys
# SMTP_HOST=smtp-relay.brevo.com
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_USER=your-brevo-login
# SMTP_PASS=your-brevo-smtp-key
# FROM_EMAIL="SignFlow <verified-sender@yourdomain.com>"

# Public URL of the app — used to build the signing links in emails and the
# Google/Microsoft redirect URIs. Locally keep localhost; after deploying, set
# it to your public URL.
APP_URL=http://localhost:4000

# PORT=4000

# --- Hosting ---
# Persistent data folder (hosting: the mounted disk). Locally defaults to ~/SignFlowData.
# STORAGE_DIR=/opt/render/project/src/server/data-disk
# Encryption key for everything at rest. Set this in the host's secret store.
# SIGNFLOW_SECRET=a-long-random-string
# Mark cookies Secure once the app is served over https:
# COOKIE_SECURE=1
# Behind a reverse proxy / load balancer (automatic on Render):
# TRUST_PROXY=1
# Turn off background jobs (reminders, expiry, webhook retries) — tests only:
# DISABLE_SCHEDULER=1

# ============================================================
# Sign-in options (all optional; the login page shows only what's configured)
# ============================================================

# --- Email one-time code ("log in with a code") ---
# Needs no extra setup: it uses the SMTP settings above. While developing
# without SMTP you can print codes to the server console instead:
# OTP_DEV_LOG=1

# NOTE: the Google and Microsoft apps below are PLATFORM apps, registered once
# by the operator. They power both "Sign in with …" and "Connect your account"
# (send from the user's inbox, save to their drive). Customers never configure
# anything. Register BOTH redirect URIs per provider:
#   {APP_URL}/api/auth/sso/<provider>/callback      (sign-in)
#   {APP_URL}/api/connect/<provider>/callback       (connect inbox + drive)

# --- Google sign-in + Gmail/Drive connections ---
# Google Cloud console → APIs & Services → Credentials → Create credentials →
# OAuth client ID → Web application. Add this Authorized redirect URI:
#   {APP_URL}/api/auth/sso/google/callback
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=xxxxxxxx.apps.googleusercontent.com
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=GOCSPX-xxxxxxxx

# --- Microsoft sign-in + Outlook/OneDrive connections (Microsoft 365 / Entra ID) ---
# For a public product set "Supported account types" to multi-tenant and
# MS_TENANT=common. For one company, use its tenant ID.
# entra.microsoft.com → App registrations → New registration → platform "Web",
# redirect URI {APP_URL}/api/auth/sso/microsoft/callback → then
# Certificates & secrets → New client secret (copy the VALUE, not the ID).
# MS_TENANT: your Directory (tenant) ID to allow only your organisation's
# accounts, "organizations" for any work account, or "common" for any account.
# MS_CLIENT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
# MS_CLIENT_SECRET=xxxxxxxx
# MS_TENANT=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

# --- Who may create an account via Google/Microsoft/code ---
# Comma-separated email domains. Leave unset to allow anyone. Existing accounts
# and password signup are unaffected.
# SSO_ALLOWED_DOMAINS=softshala.com

# ============================================================
# OneDrive / SharePoint archive (optional)
# ============================================================
# When a document is completed, its sealed PDF (with certificate + audit trail)
# is copied to Microsoft 365 automatically. Uses the SAME app registration as
# Microsoft sign-in (MS_TENANT / MS_CLIENT_ID / MS_CLIENT_SECRET above).
#
# One-time setup in entra.microsoft.com → App registrations → SignFlow →
# API permissions → Add a permission → Microsoft Graph → APPLICATION permissions:
#   Files.ReadWrite.All   if archiving to a user's OneDrive  (ONEDRIVE_USER)
#   Sites.ReadWrite.All   if archiving to a SharePoint site  (ONEDRIVE_SITE)
# then "Grant admin consent".
#
# Destination — set ONE of these:
#   One central OneDrive. Files land in  SignFlow/<sender name>/<date>_<time>_<signer>.pdf
#   and each sender's folder is shared read-only with that sender, so every
#   person sees only their own documents while the owner sees everything:
# ONEDRIVE_USER=shubham@softshala.com
#   Or: each sender's OWN OneDrive (sender must be a user in your tenant):
# ONEDRIVE_USER=@sender
#   Or: a SharePoint site library (same layout and sharing):
# ONEDRIVE_SITE=softshala.sharepoint.com/sites/Contracts
#
# Root folder inside that drive (created automatically; default "SignFlow"):
# ONEDRIVE_FOLDER=SignFlow
# Folder/file naming. Slashes make sub-folders; ".pdf" is added automatically.
# Tokens: {sender_name} {sender_email} {folder} {title} {id} {date} {time}
#         {signer} {signer_first} {signer_last} {signers}
# ONEDRIVE_PATH={sender_name}/{date}_{time}_{signer}
# Timezone used for {date} and {time} (completion time):
# ONEDRIVE_TIMEZONE=Asia/Kolkata
# Set to 0 if you don't want each sender's folder shared with them automatically:
# ONEDRIVE_SHARE_WITH_SENDER=1

# ============================================================
# Claude: in-app assistant + MCP server
# ============================================================
# SignFlow exposes an MCP server at {APP_URL}/mcp (OAuth for claude.ai
# connectors, or an API key as Bearer for Claude Desktop / Claude Code).
# Nothing to configure for that. The in-app "✨ Ask" assistant runs on each
# user's OWN Anthropic API key (entered in Settings → Claude & MCP), or a
# workspace key set by an admin — so customers pay for their own usage.
# Only if YOU want to pay for everyone, set both of these:
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# ASSISTANT_SHARED_KEY=1
# ASSISTANT_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5
